  "solution": "**Given:**\n\ncos θ = 5/13\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nsin²θ + cos²θ = 1\n\nValue of √((1 - sin θ)/(1 + sin θ)) = ?\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nsin²θ + cos²θ = 1\n\n⇒ sin²θ = 1 - cos²θ\n\n⇒ sin²θ = 1 - (5/13)²\n\n⇒ sin²θ = 1 - 25/169\n\n⇒ sin²θ = (169 - 25)/169\n\n⇒ sin²θ = 144/169\n\n⇒ sin θ = √(144/169)\n\n⇒ sin θ = 12/13\n\nNow, √((1 - sin θ)/(1 + sin θ))\n\n⇒ √((1 - 12/13)/(1 + 12/13))\n\n⇒ √((13/13 - 12/13)/(13/13 + 12/13))\n\n⇒ √((1/13)/(25/13))\n\n⇒ √(1/25)\n\n⇒ 1/5\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**",
